lambda Expression:
-anonymous function
-not having any name
-not having any return type
-not having modifier

public class Main{
private void SayHello(){
sout("hello...");
}
}

steps to make any fun lambda expression
1.remove modifier
2.remove return type
3.remove method name
4.place arrow

example 1:
private void sayHello(){
sout("hello");
}

|to

()->{System.out.println("hello....");}

example 2:
private void add(int a,int b){
sout(a+b);
}

|to

(int a, int b)->{System.out.println(a+b);}


modifier,name,return type=remove =>lambda expression

characteristic:
1.If body has just one statement then we can remove curly brackets
private int getStringLength(String str){
return str.length();
}

|to

(String str)->return str.length()}

|to

(String str)-> return str.length();


2.use type inference, compiler guess the situation or context
private void add(int a,int b){
sout("hello");
}

|to
(int a,int b)->{sout(a+b);}

|to

(a,b)->sout(a+b);

3.no return keyword
private int getStringLength(String str){
return str.length();
}

|to

(String str)->{return str.length();}

|to

(str)->str.legth();

4.single parameter , skip curly braces

(str)->str.length();

|to

str->str.length();

